Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Clip mode: a queued clip blinks at the beat rate from
 the first blink.

Loopy flashes a queued clip itself (colour, then off, about every 100 ms).
The firmware sets the queued state only after two off-to-on toggles.
Before that, each off cleared the cell, so the pad showed the first Loopy flashes at 100 ms.
Now an off less than SMK_APC40_TOGGLE_TICKS (256 ms) after an on keeps the colour.
smk_apc40_cells_age clears the cell if no on comes in that time.
An off after a long steady colour, or an off after an off, clears the cell at once as before.
tests/smk_apc40_map_test.c makes sure that the first blink period is one beat at 120 and 90 BPM, and 500 ms with no clock.
